Z||000000||mrgone||07-11-2001||02:50 PM||||well i took off my intake and compared it to the one in the haynes manual and noticed that my damper door is missing, and the little rubber thing it sits on has the hole melted to a small hole, constantley letting hot air in regardless of the temp.<BR>the door is supposed to open when oil temp falls below 86F.<P>this is prolly a hack fix for my missing oil temperature sender.<P>sooo.... what should i do? will this harm my engine in any way? the rad fan is wired to the heater blower controls and i usually have that on high. and my guages dont work.<P>it would be easier to find an intake from a junker, but the junk yard would charge me 50$ for the thing prolly. and my intake is kinda in rough shape anyway.<P>anyway i was looking for the IAC valve to clean it and someone sent me a pic of where it should be, and my EGR is in the same spot. so i dont know where the IAC is.<P>the EGR is more important though, cause of my bad milage. anyone know what i have to go through to repair it?<BR>IAC only affects cold mornings. EGR is making bad bad gas milage.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-11-2001||05:35 PM||||I don't recall the fieros being equipped with an oil temp sensor.  Don't you mean coolant temp sensor?  Also, what engine do you have 4 or 6 cyl.  If it is a 6 cyl the IAC is on the opposite side of the cable side of the throttle body.  The egr sits on the exhaust cross-over pipe and is located near the coil and distributor.<P><BR>||||reg||1
